1
00:00:00,265 --> 00:00:03,145
(Penny:)Your friend's really cute.
Anything going on with you two?

2
00:00:03,685 --> 00:00:04,815
Leslie?

3
00:00:04,978 --> 00:00:07,268
No, no. What, are you kidding?

4
00:00:07,439 --> 00:00:10,439
(Sheldon:)He asked her out once.
It was an embarrassing failure.

5
00:00:10,775 --> 00:00:11,815
(Leonard:)Thank you, Sheldon.

6
00:00:11,985 --> 00:00:14,155
(Leonard:)I'm sorry.
Was that supposed to be a secret?

7
00:00:15,363 --> 00:00:18,113
(Penny:)That's too bad.
You guys would make a cute couple.

8
00:00:19,784 --> 00:00:21,574
- Oh, dear.
- What's the matter?

9
00:00:21,745 --> 00:00:22,915
(Raj:)She didn't take my order.

10
00:00:23,079 --> 00:00:26,289
How could she take your order
when you're too neurotic to talk to her?

11
00:00:27,083 --> 00:00:30,463
(Raj:)Nevertheless,
this will be reflected in her tip.

12
00:00:32,964 --> 00:00:35,964
LEONARD: What did Penny mean,
"you'd make a cute couple"?

13
00:00:36,134 --> 00:00:37,804
(Sheldon:)I assume she meant
the two of you...

14
00:00:37,969 --> 00:00:41,509
(Sheldon:)...would constitute a couple
that others might consider cute.

15
00:00:43,141 --> 00:00:47,851
An alternate and less likely interpretation
is that you could manufacture one.

16
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:51,730
As in, "Look, Leonard and Leslie
made Mr. and Mrs. Goldfarb.

17
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:53,690
Aren't they adorable?"

18
00:00:53,860 --> 00:00:56,450
(Leonard:)If Penny didn't know
that Leslie had turned me down...

19
00:00:56,613 --> 00:01:00,823
...then that would mean that she, Penny,
thought I should ask her, Leslie, out...

20
00:01:00,992 --> 00:01:03,832
...indicating that Penny had no interest
in me asking her out.

21
00:01:03,995 --> 00:01:06,335
(Leonard:)But because she did know
I had asked Leslie out...

22
00:01:06,498 --> 00:01:08,578
...and that she, Leslie,
had turned me down...

23
00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:12,170
(Leonard:)...then she, Penny,
could be offering consolation.

24
00:01:13,546 --> 00:01:16,336
"That's too bad,
you would have made a cute couple."

25
00:01:16,508 --> 00:01:20,928
(Leonard:)But while thinking,
"Good, Leonard remains available."

26
00:01:22,055 --> 00:01:24,435
(Sheldon:)You're a lucky man, Leonard.

27
00:01:25,684 --> 00:01:26,724
(Leonard:)How so?

28
00:01:26,893 --> 00:01:29,143
(Sheldon:)You're talking to one of
the three men in the West...

29
00:01:29,312 --> 00:01:31,732
(Sheldon:)...capable of following
that train of thought.

30
00:01:32,857 --> 00:01:33,987
Well, what do you think?

31
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:38,030
(Sheldon:)I said I could follow it,
I didn't say I cared.

